---
# Catch2's TEST_CASE/SECTION/REQUIRE macros expand into nested lambdas;
# clang-tidy attributes their combined complexity to a synthetic
# "dummyFunctionN" and prints the whole macro-expansion backtrace through
# test/catch2/catch_amalgamated.hpp as context. That's noise, not a real
# finding, and only happens in test files -- so disable it here, not in the
# root .clang-tidy which still applies to src/.
#
# SECTION() also expands to an `if` with an initializer, a C++17 feature
# clang accepts under -std=c++14 as a harmless extension (the real test
# build compiles it fine, see test/Makefile). clang-diagnostic-c++17-extensions
# fires on every SECTION/REQUIRE call site otherwise, purely from the
# project's C++14 baseline, not a real issue -- disable it here too.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -clang-diagnostic-c++17-extensions
